+## selection2env Catalog Sources
+
+`generate_scene/catalog_sources.py` normalizes three candidate sources without
+weakening the RoboTwin execution gate:
+
+- RoboTwin discovered object directories are execution-eligible.
+- `asset_catalogs/agenticsim_placement_assets.json` snapshots the existing
+  AgenticSim placement-agent aliases. An alias is eligible only when its
+  `backend_asset_id` exists in the active RoboTwin catalog.
+- Articraft-10K metadata is searchable, but each result stays
+  `catalog_only_not_imported` until a separate URDF/import/physics probe passes.
+
+Search all three sources and write the RoboTwin execution catalog:
+
+```bash
+python3 generate_scene/catalog_sources.py \
+  --prompt "open the drawer and place the mug inside" \
+  --robotwin-catalog runs/catalog/robotwin_discovered.json \
+  --agenticsim-catalog asset_catalogs/agenticsim_placement_assets.json \
+  --articraft-manifest /path/to/articraft10k_manifest.json \
+  --out runs/catalog/drawer_mug_candidates.json \
+  --execution-catalog-out runs/catalog/robotwin_with_agenticsim_aliases.json
+```
+
+The main scene pipeline accepts the same optional AgenticSim and Articraft
+paths through `--agenticsim-catalog` and `--articraft-manifest`. It writes
+`catalog_candidate_search.json` beside the normal scene-generation artifacts.
+
+Run the pure catalog tests with:
+
+```bash
+python3 -m pip install -e ".[test]"
+python3 -m pytest -q
+```
+
 ## One Command

